<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">12 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 12 September, from 490 BCE to 1962.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/athens" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/athens.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">490 BCE <span class="tih-ago">2,515 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Athenians defeat the Persians at Marathon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">By the traditional date, the Athenians and Plataeans charged and routed the Persian landing force at Marathon. The legend of a runner carrying news to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> inspired the modern marathon race.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1185">1185 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">841 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Isaac II Angelos is crowned Byzantine emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a revolt deposed Andronikos I Komnenos, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isaac-ii-angelos">Isaac II Angelos</a> was crowned emperor, the crowd having rejected the coronation of his uncle John Doukas. Isaac established the Angelos family as the new imperial dynasty.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isaac-ii-angelos">Isaac II Angelos</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1213">1213 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">813 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Simon de Montfort defeats and kills Peter II of Aragon at Muret</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusaders</a> under Simon de Montfort routed a larger army of Aragon and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a> at Muret, killing King Peter II. The defeat ended Aragonese hopes in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/languedoc">Languedoc</a> and opened it to northern French rule.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1229">1229 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">797 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">James I of Aragon's army fights the Battle of Portopí</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-i-of-aragon">James I of Aragon</a>'s army fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> troops holding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallorca">Mallorca</a> at Portopí, between Santa Ponsa and the City of Majorca, in the second major battle of his campaign to conquer the island. James conquered Mallorca that year.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-i-of-aragon">James I of Aragon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallorca">Mallorca</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1297">1297 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">729 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Portugal and Castile fix their border in the Treaty of Alcañices</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a treaty mediated by the pope and signed at Alcañices in León, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denis-rapontchombo">King Denis</a> of Portugal and Ferdinand IV of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> agreed peace and royal marriages, and Portugal gained the Riba-Côa district. The border it fixed has changed little since.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-alcanices">Treaty of Alcañices</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denis-of-portugal">Denis of Portugal</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1683">1683 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">343 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John III Sobieski relieves the siege of Vienna</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A relief army led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> III Sobieski of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> routed the Ottoman forces besieging <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>, ending with a great charge of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-hussars">Polish hussars</a>. The Ottoman advance into central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> was halted for good.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-hussars">Polish hussars</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1848">1848 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">178 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Switzerland adopts its federal constitution</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Swiss Diet declared the new federal constitution accepted, turning a loose league of cantons into a federal state with a two-chamber parliament. Its framework still underpins <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> today.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1962">1962 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">64 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Kennedy tells Rice University 'we choose to go to the Moon'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a speech at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">Rice</a> University in Houston, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-f-kennedy">John F. Kennedy</a> committed America to a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhu">Moon</a> landing that decade, 'not because they are easy, but because they are hard'. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a> 11 landed seven years later.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 12 September <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hsinbyushin"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Hsinbyushin</span><span class="tp">1736–1776</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pedro-albizu-campos"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pedro-albizu-campos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pedro Albizu Campos</span><span class="tp">1891–1965</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/juscelino-kubitschek"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/juscelino-kubitschek.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Juscelino Kubitschek</span><span class="tp">1902–1976</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/amilcar-cabral"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/amilcar-cabral.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Amílcar Cabral</span><span class="tp">1924–1973</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 12 September <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/peter-ii-of-aragon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/peter-ii-of-aragon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Peter II of Aragon</span><span class="tp">1178–1213</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/henri-coiffier-de-ruze-marquis-of-cinq-mars"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henri-coiffier-de-ruze-marquis-of-cinq-mars.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Henri Coiffier de Ruzé, Marquis of Cinq-Mars</span><span class="tp">1620–1642</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gebhard-leberecht-von-blucher"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gebhard-leberecht-von-blucher.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gebhard Leberecht von Blücher</span><span class="tp">1742–1819</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francois-guizot"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francois-guizot.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">François Guizot</span><span class="tp">1787–1874</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/steve-biko"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/steve-biko.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Steve Biko</span><span class="tp">1946–1977</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ernesto-geisel"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ernesto-geisel.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ernesto Geisel</span><span class="tp">1907–1996</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
